S1945:
## 13. Stop condition

Stop and request synchronization/ruling if:

* a new theoretical claim is required;
* an OQ must change status;
* an evidence class must be upgraded;
* a governance contradiction must be resolved;
* 𝒪_core must be authoritatively frozen;
* a formal construct must be changed rather than merely documented;
* existing accepted Part II wording would need historical alteration;
* the distinction between formal, computational, empirical and governance closure becomes ambiguous.

## 2. Do not restart theory discovery

Do NOT:

* start another unrestricted gap-discovery pass;
* invent new theoretical constructs;
* declare the theory complete;
* promote an OQ without an authorized ruling;
* upgrade an evidence class merely because a verification artifact exists;
* treat a verification session's conclusion as automatically book-authoritative;
* modify ratified architecture or governance decisions;
* resolve governance questions yourself.

